Because of Python doesn’t have conditional compile so I usually have to write something like
if __debug__:
    do_some_code_with_debugger
else:
    do_some_code

Doing things this way not only cause larger bytecodes but also unnecessarily embed the debug clause in the released code. I haven’t find a proper solution for this situation yet.

